-- Codex Insurance Limited -- Hospital Income Policy
--
-- Isomorphic encoding of the contract in fixtures/chubb-policy.txt.
-- Rules only -- no claim data is defined in this file (see apply.l4).
--
-- Modelling notes (see NOTES.md for the full list of judgement calls):
--   * Per the task brief, signing (S1.1(1)) and timely premium payment (S1.1(2)) are
--     ASSUMED true for every claim and are therefore not modelled as rules.
--   * Per the task brief, every date/time relevant to a claim (other than the
--     claimant's age) is given relative to the policy's effective date. So every
--     temporal fact below is a NUMBER of months elapsed since the effective date,
--     and no calendar-date arithmetic (daydate/YMD) is needed anywhere in this file.

§ `Defined terms`

DECLARE Claim HAS
    -- S1.3 -- the wellness-visit condition
    `wellness visit occurred by month`                IS A NUMBER
        -- months after the effective date that the medical wellness visit itself took place
    `wellness visit confirmation supplied by month`   IS A NUMBER
        -- months after the effective date that written confirmation of that visit was
        -- supplied by You to the Company

    -- S1.2 -- cancellation ground: fraud / misrepresentation / material withholding
    `fraud or misrepresentation`                      IS A BOOLEAN

    -- S4.6 / S1.1 -- timing of the hospitalization giving rise to the claim
    `hospitalization occurs by month`                 IS A NUMBER
        -- months after the effective date that the hospitalization (confinement) began

    -- S2 -- the benefit trigger
    `confined due to sickness or injury`              IS A BOOLEAN
        -- confined in a hospital as a result of sickness or accidental Injury (S2.1)
    `hospital located in the United States`           IS A BOOLEAN
        -- S2.2 restricts the Daily Hospital Income Benefit to confinement in a hospital
        -- in the United States
    `claim made to the Company`                       IS A BOOLEAN
        -- S2.3 -- a claim was made to the Company setting out the basis for the claim

    -- S3.1 -- general exclusions, items 1-4: causal ("arising ... out of") grounds
    `sickness or injury arose from skydiving`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `sickness or injury arose from service in the military`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `sickness or injury arose from service as a fire fighter`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `sickness or injury arose from service in the police`        IS A BOOLEAN

    -- S3.1, item 5 -- age-based exclusion (a standalone bar, not an "arising out of" ground)
    `age at the time of hospitalization`              IS A NUMBER


§ `Section 1 -- Policy in effect and conditions`

§§ `1.3 -- the wellness-visit condition`

-- "No later than the 7th month anniversary ... you will supply us with written
-- confirmation ... of a wellness visit ... occurring no later than the 6th month
-- anniversary of the effective date of this policy."
--
-- Both the visit itself (<= 6 months) and the supply of written confirmation of it
-- (<= 7 months) are required. Every claim in this benchmark reports these as completed,
-- historical facts relative to the effective date (never as an open/indeterminate
-- status), so the alternative limb of S1.1(3) ("... is still pending or has been
-- satisfied ...") never has independent effect here: a confirmation reported as
-- supplied at month M is, by that very fact, already at or past month M, so "still
-- pending" cannot rescue a confirmation reported late. See NOTES.md.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 1.3 condition has been satisfied in a timely fashion` claim IF
        claim's `wellness visit occurred by month`              AT MOST 6
    AND claim's `wellness visit confirmation supplied by month` AT MOST 7


§§ `1.1 / 4.6 -- the policy term`

-- "will last for a period of one year from that date"
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the hospitalization occurs within the one-year policy term` claim IF
    claim's `hospitalization occurs by month` AT MOST 12


§§ `1.2 -- cancellation`

-- "Cancelation will be deemed to have occurred if there is fraud, or any
-- misrepresentation or material withholding of any information ..., or if the
-- condition set out in Section 1.3 has not been satisfied in a timely fashion. It
-- will also be automatically canceled ... on the last day of the policy term ..."
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the policy has been canceled` claim IF
        claim's `fraud or misrepresentation`
    OR  NOT `the section 1.3 condition has been satisfied in a timely fashion` claim
    OR  NOT `the hospitalization occurs within the one-year policy term` claim


§§ `1.1 -- policy in effect`

-- "The payment of any benefit under this policy is conditioned on the policy being in
-- effect at the time of the hospitalization ... The policy will be in effect if: 1.
-- This agreement is signed [ASSUMED], 2. The applicable premium ... has been paid
-- [ASSUMED], 3. The condition set out in Section 1.3 is still pending or has been
-- satisfied ..., and 4. The policy has not been canceled."
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the policy is in effect at the time of the hospitalization` claim IF
    NOT `the policy has been canceled` claim


§ `Section 2 -- Benefits`

-- "If you have been confined in a hospital as a result of sickness or accidental
-- Injury, we will pay you the Daily Hospital Income Benefit ... will only be payable
-- for each (24 hour) day of continuous confinement in a hospital in the United States
-- ... To trigger any benefit, a claim must be made to the Company ..."
--
-- The 365-day cap and the $500/day amount (S2.2, S5.1) govern only the *quantum* of
-- the benefit, not whether the policy applies to the claim, so they are not modelled:
-- none of the benchmark questions ask about duration or amount.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the benefit conditions of section 2 are met` claim IF
        claim's `confined due to sickness or injury`
    AND claim's `hospital located in the United States`
    AND claim's `claim made to the Company`


§ `Section 3 -- General exclusions`

-- "Your policy will not apply to, and no benefit will be paid with respect to, any
-- event causing sickness or accidental injury arising directly or indirectly out of:
-- 1. Skydiving; or 2. Service in the military; or 3. Service as a fire fighter; or 4.
-- Service in the police; or 5. If your age at the time of the hospitalization is equal
-- to or greater than 80 years of age."
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a general exclusion applies` claim IF
        claim's `sickness or injury arose from skydiving`
    OR  claim's `sickness or injury arose from service in the military`
    OR  claim's `sickness or injury arose from service as a fire fighter`
    OR  claim's `sickness or injury arose from service in the police`
    OR  claim's `age at the time of hospitalization` AT LEAST 80


§ `Top-level coverage decision`

-- Combines S1 (policy in effect), S2 (the benefit is triggered) and S3 (no exclusion
-- bars the claim) into the single yes/no question the benchmark asks: "will my policy
-- apply?"
@export Decide whether a claim is covered under the Codex Insurance Limited hospital income policy
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE covered claim IF
        `the policy is in effect at the time of the hospitalization` claim
    AND `the benefit conditions of section 2 are met` claim
    AND NOT `a general exclusion applies` claim
